WP10.8 -- the three XsRecon sites call the counter by the name of what it counts.

WHY THIS IS A PATCH FILE AND NOT A COMMIT.  src/CudaXsReconBackend.cu is held by
the concurrent WP21-B2/C2 arm.  This diff is written against the file as it
stands on codex/exact-throughput-campaign at 43f8174, and is to be applied after
that arm lands:

    git apply --3way docs/patches/wp10_8_xsrecon.patch

NOTHING BEHAVES DIFFERENTLY EITHER WAY, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE.  WP10.8 renamed
`blockpool::Stats::arena_rebuilds` to `block_reshapes` and kept
`noteArenaRebuild()` as an inline alias of the new `noteBlockReshape()` -- the
alias exists precisely so this file (and GpuPhysicsArenaCuda.cu) could keep
compiling untouched while it was held by another arm.  The tree passes
`tools/test_arena_persist_contract.py` and
`tools/test_device_block_pool_contract.py` before and after this patch.

WHAT WAS WRONG WITH THE NAME.  The 238 block-38 phase-2 soak read `arena_rebuilds`
climbing +17 per generation -- at width 16 with one promote, exactly one per
CASE -- and it did so in BOTH arms, with `RASBERY_ARENA_PERSIST` off and on.  The
report concluded that "`RASBERY_ARENA_PERSIST=1` is not preventing rebuilds the
way its name promises".  It never promised that.  The three sites below fire when
a per-INSTANCE device region is freed and re-laid-out because its SHAPE changed
under it -- `Impl::ensure()` when `want_nxyz != nxyz`, the node table when
`n_nodes > nodes_cap`, the stream arrays when `stream_len > stream_cap` -- which
is a backend instance standing its blocks up at its first real geometry, once per
case, and is not an arena teardown at all.  The persist flag pools the BLOCKS
those sites release; it was never going to stop the sites firing.

The number is real and worth keeping.  It is now called `block_reshapes`, and the
receipt's `arena_rebuilds` field carries the thing its own name always promised:
process-lifetime (`poolable=false`) regions handed back, derived inside the pool
from the registration flag with no call site cooperating.  Between generations
that is 0, and a nonzero one IS the arena teardown the VRAM sawtooth raised.

--- a/src/CudaXsReconBackend.cu
+++ b/src/CudaXsReconBackend.cu
@@
         rasbery::AllocWindow _alloc_window("xsrecon.instance.regrow");
-        // WP10.6.  A REBUILD is a live region freed and re-laid-out under a
-        // shape change; a first stand-up is not one.  The distinction is the
-        // whole question the VRAM sawtooth raised -- "is the arena torn down
-        // per generation?" -- and it is now a counter in the MEM receipt
-        // instead of an inference from a board-level memory trace.
-        if (dev_block != nullptr) rasbery::gpu::blockpool::noteArenaRebuild();
+        // WP10.8.  A RESHAPE is a live PER-INSTANCE region freed and re-laid-out
+        // under a shape change; a first stand-up is not one.  This fires about
+        // once per case, in both arms -- it is this backend instance sizing its
+        // blocks to the deck's geometry, not an arena teardown.  WP10.6 called
+        // it `noteArenaRebuild()` and the 238 block-38 report read the resulting
+        // `arena_rebuilds=+17/generation` as evidence that RASBERY_ARENA_PERSIST
+        // was failing.  The counter now has the name of what it counts, and the
+        // receipt's `arena_rebuilds` answers the arena question separately.
+        if (dev_block != nullptr) rasbery::gpu::blockpool::noteBlockReshape();
         if (dev_block) { rasbery::gpu::deviceBlockFree(dev_block); dev_block = nullptr; }
@@
         rasbery::AllocWindow _alloc_window("xsrecon.nodes.regrow");
-        if (d.dev_nodes != nullptr) rasbery::gpu::blockpool::noteArenaRebuild();
+        if (d.dev_nodes != nullptr) rasbery::gpu::blockpool::noteBlockReshape();
         if (d.dev_nodes) rasbery::gpu::deviceBlockFree(d.dev_nodes);
@@
         rasbery::AllocWindow _alloc_window("xsrecon.stream.regrow");
-        if (d.dev_sdid != nullptr) rasbery::gpu::blockpool::noteArenaRebuild();
+        if (d.dev_sdid != nullptr) rasbery::gpu::blockpool::noteBlockReshape();
         if (d.dev_sdid) rasbery::gpu::deviceBlockFree(d.dev_sdid);

